        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "936dddfd-48b1-5dee-8e2d-76adc78f10b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Bowles, Sir Desmond Lorenz de Silva, Geoffrey Dobbs, Maurice Talvande (Count de Mauny)\n- Places: Taprobane Island, Sri Lanka\n- Roles: author, composer, translator, Chief Prosecutor, businessman, landscaper, furniture-maker\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Talvande, Count de Mauny Talvande, lived from 1866 to 1941 and was a French-born naturalised British landscaper, furniture-maker, and self-inventor.\n- Maurice Talvande is best known as the owner and recreator of Taprobane Island in Sri Lanka.\n- Paul Frederic Bowles lived from December 30, 1910 to November 18, 1999 and was an American expatriate composer, author, and translator.\n- Taprobane Island passed to Paul Bowles, then to the Sri Lankan-born former UN Chief Prosecutor Sir Desmond Lorenz de Silva, and later to the Australian businessman Geoffrey Dobbs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
